  "interpretation": [
    "All four affirmative requests received clarification. Three of their four reference areas already contained a two-view OPEN point from the actual local model.",
    "A passenger who selected the gravel area and the interiors of both marked rows could save the exact point. The smooth lay-by was classified as through-lane and rejected. None of these mark checks produced an automatic destination or measured the full vehicle footprint.",
    "All six centre-lane marks and both explicitly prohibited-target marks withheld. In the two natural negative cases the app returned a generic request to tap an off-lane spot; it did not identify the crossing or lorry lane. The stripe request returned no selectable bays and asked for a smaller interior tap.",
    "The three native pull-in geometry methods produced zero candidates on all six originals. N01 is a ground-supply limitation. N03, N04 and N06 already had candidate supply in the requested region. Their specific language/landmark constraints were not established or applied. In N04 the destination parser explicitly rejects the phrase ‘across from’, including when it describes a landmark across the street rather than the destination."
